pozhenzi.translation:
Drunk, I trim the lamp and look at my sword;
in dream I am back to horns sounding through the linked camps.
Roast meat is shared out beneath the banners across eight hundred li;
fifty strings play music of the frontier;
on the field in autumn the troops are reviewed.
The horse flies fast as the Dilu;
the bow twangs like thunder and startles the string.
To finish the lord's task of the realm,
to win a name in life and after death -
alas, white hair has grown.

huanxisha.translation:
A new song, a cup of wine;
the weather of last year, the same old pond and terrace.
The sun is setting in the west - when will it return?
Flowers fall, and nothing can be done;
swallows come back, as though I knew them,
and I pace alone on the little garden's scented path.

chaitoufeng.translation:
Red, soft hands, yellow-sealed wine,
spring colour fills the city, willows over the palace wall.
The east wind was cruel, joy was thin;
a heart full of sorrow, years of separation and loneliness -
wrong! wrong! wrong!
Spring is as before, but you are thin for nothing;
tear marks, red, soak through your mermaid-silk handkerchief.
Peach blossoms fall, the pond and pavilion are idle;
the mountain vows still stand, but a brocade letter is hard to send -
let it be! let it be! let it be!

linjiangxian_yan.translation:
After the dream, the tower is locked high;
when the wine wears off, the curtains hang low.
Last year's spring sorrow has come again.
Fallen flowers, a person standing alone;
fine rain, a pair of swallows flying.
I remember when I first saw Little Ping,
in a gauze dress with a double heart-character.
On the pipa strings she spoke of her longing;
the bright moon was there then,
and once lit her going home like a coloured cloud.

zhegutian_yan.translation:
Coloured sleeves, so eagerly offering the jade cup;
in those days I was ready to drink till my face turned red.
Dancing low, the willow-tower moon sank;
singing on, until the wind from the peach-blossom fan was spent.
Since we parted, I have remembered meeting;
how many times in dreams I was with you.
Tonight I hold the silver lamp up to look at you,
still afraid that this meeting is only a dream.
